@page
@inject IOptions<SiteSettings> SiteOptions
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Rules";
}

<h1 class="h4 mb-4">Server rules</h1>

<div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h5">Gameplay</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Players are expected to play fair and to respect each other.</li>
            <li>Exploiting bugs, using cheats, bots or macros that automate gameplay is prohibited.</li>
            <li>Exploiting a bug to duplicate items or crash the server is grounds for an immediate ban.</li>
            <li>In-game name, guild name and store name must not contain offensive content.</li>
            <li>Account sharing is at your own risk - the account owner is responsible for everything done with the account.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Resets and statistics</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Resets are done in-game with the <code>/reset</code> command at level 400.</li>
            <li>Each reset grants a new pool of stat points based on the server configuration.</li>
            <li>Stat points can be distributed with <code>/autostat</code> or manually.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Your account</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Never give your password or security code to anyone - not even staff. Staff never asks for them.</li>
            <li>The security code is required in-game for character deletion and guild kicks. Keep it secret.</li>
            <li>Lost access to your account? Only the registered e-mail or a direct request to the administration can help.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-muted small mt-4">
            @SiteOptions.Value.Name is a private, non-commercial game server, not affiliated with Webzen Inc.
            The administration reserves the right to modify these rules at any time and to take action at its
            own discretion in cases not covered here.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
